.Dd July 19, 2026
.Dt AUTHORITYD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm authorityd
.Nd capability authority daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl b Ar bootstrap
.Op Fl f Ar conffile
.Op Fl p Ar pidfile
.Op Fl T
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the system authority daemon for the capability world.
It claims system resources exclusively via the
.Xr mac_capability 4
MAC capability, protects its own integrity via
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4 ,
and manages a single bootstrap child process, typically
.Xr serviced 8 ,
which reads capability bundles and supervises individual services.
.Pp
.Nm
is installed both as
.Pa /usr/sbin/authorityd
and as
.Pa /sbin/authority-init .
The latter is the system PID 1 program: the installed loader configuration
places it first in
.Va init_path ,
with the stock
.Pa /sbin/init
and rescue init programs as execution fallbacks.
When invoked as PID 1,
.Nm
does not daemonize; it runs the Authority init state machine, starts
.Xr serviced 8
as its first managed child, and remains the system lifecycle authority.
.Pp
.Nm
does not start or manage services directly.
It mints capability tokens on request from
.Xr serviced 8
via the authority protocol, a message-passing channel over a mac_capability
channel descriptor.
.Pp
During startup,
.Nm
executes the following phases:
.Bl -enum
.It
Load configuration from
.Pa /etc/authorityd.conf
(or the path given with
.Fl f ) ,
open syslog, acquire pidfile.
.It
Daemonize (unless
.Fl d
or
.Fl T
is given).
.It
Harden the process via
.Xr procctl 2
(subtree reaper, OOM protection, trace disable, signal-exit logging).
.It
Open
.Pa /dev/mac_capability
and claim configured resources via the
.Xr mac_capability_isolation 4
service.
.It
Claim system gates via the
.Xr mac_capability_system 4
service.
.It
Activate the
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4
shield with the flags specified in the configuration file.
.It
Create a control socket for administrative commands.
.It
Start
.Xr serviced 8
as a single child process via
.Xr pdfork 2 .
The resulting process descriptor is restricted to supervision rights and
irreversibly confined against descriptor transfer, fork inheritance, and exec
inheritance.
Possession of this descriptor is the sole explicit signal authority over the
protected service manager.
.It
Enter the event loop, monitoring the serviced process descriptor
and control socket connections via
.Xr kqueue 2 .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-b bootstrap"
.It Fl b Ar bootstrap
Start
.Ar bootstrap
as the first managed process instead of the configured
.Va service_manager .
.It Fl d
Run in the foreground and log to standard error as well as syslog.
.It Fl f Ar conffile
Read configuration from
.Ar conffile
instead of
.Pa /etc/authorityd.conf .
.It Fl p Ar pidfile
Write the process ID to
.Ar pidfile
instead of the configured pidfile path.
Overrides the
.Va pidfile
setting in the configuration file.
.It Fl T
Test mode.
Run in the foreground without daemonizing, without
.Xr mac_capability 4
or control socket hardening.
Manifests are parsed but services are not launched.
Intended for automated tests.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
reads its configuration from
.Pa /etc/authorityd.conf
in UCL format.
The configuration file is optional \(em if it does not exist,
compiled-in defaults are used.
Syntax errors are fatal.
.Pp
The following keys are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "serviced_control_socket"
.It Va pidfile
Path to the pidfile.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/authorityd.pid .
.It Va control_socket
Path to the control socket.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/authorityd.sock .
.It Va control_socket_mode
File mode for the control socket.
Default: 0700 (root only).
.It Va service_manager
Path to the first managed process started by
.Nm
at bootstrap.
Default:
.Pa /usr/libexec/serviced .
If empty, no service manager is started.
May be overridden with
.Fl b .
.It Va serviced_control_socket
Path to the control socket for
.Xr serviced 8 .
Passed via the
.Ev SERVICED_CONTROL_SOCKET
environment variable.
Default: empty.
.El
.Ss Integrity
The
.Va integrity
section controls
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4
flags that protect
.Nm
from external interference.
Each key is a boolean (true/false).
The default integrity flags are
.Dv CP_SF_PTRACE | CP_SF_SIGNAL | CP_SF_SIGKILL | CP_SF_SIGCONT |
.Dv CP_SF_WAIT | CP_SF_SCHED | CP_SF_KTRACE .
.Bl -tag -width "visible"
.It Va ptrace
Block ptrace attach from foreign nonces.
Default: true.
.It Va signal
Block all signals except SIGKILL and SIGCONT from foreign nonces.
Always enabled.
.It Va sigkill
Block SIGKILL from foreign nonces.
Always enabled.
.It Va sigcont
Block SIGCONT from foreign nonces.
Always enabled.
.It Va visible
Hide
.Nm
from
.Xr ps 1 ,
.Xr top 1 ,
and procfs enumeration.
Default: false.
.It Va wait
Block wait4 from non-parent processes.
Default: true.
.It Va sched
Block scheduler priority and CPU affinity manipulation.
Default: true.
.It Va core
Suppress core dumps to prevent leaking secrets from process memory.
Default: false.
.It Va ktrace
Block passive syscall tracing via
.Xr ktrace 1 .
Default: true.
.El
.Pp
The signal, sigkill, and sigcont protections are mandatory and cannot be
disabled by configuration.
Consequently, all foreign-nonce ambient PID signals, including signal 0,
are denied.
.Xr service 8
uses the root-only control socket for status, reload, and graceful shutdown.
An init or other supervisor may retain a process descriptor created by
.Xr pdfork 2 ;
.Xr pdkill 2
through that descriptor remains the explicit forced-termination authority.
.Ss Claims
The
.Va claims
section lists resources under authority control.
Resources listed here are
.Em policy claims :
claimed exclusively by
.Nm
at boot via the
.Xr mac_capability_isolation 4
service.
Once claimed, MACF hooks deny access from all other processes,
including root.
.Pa /dev/mac_capability
is always claimed automatically.
.Pp
Claim limits: at most 64 paths, 32 network claims, and 32 jail claims.
.Pp
.Bf -symbolic
Paths on network filesystems (NFS, FUSE) may block during
.Xr open 2
if the server is unreachable.
.Nm
opens claimed paths with
.Dv O_NONBLOCK ,
which prevents blocking on FIFOs and device nodes, but does not
help with network filesystems because the block occurs during
VFS name resolution.
To protect a network mount point without contacting the server,
claim the parent directory instead (e.g.,
.Pa /mnt
rather than
.Pa /mnt/nfs ) .
A future
.Dv FI_OP_CLAIM_PATH
operation that performs path resolution kernel-side with
.Dv NOCROSSMOUNT
would resolve this limitation.
.Ef
.Ss Dynamic Claims
Resources not pre-declared in
.Nm authorityd.conf
are
.Em auto-claimed
on the first mint request from
.Xr serviced 8 .
These
.Em dynamic claims
.Pq Dv CLAIM_SOURCE_SERVICE
are reference-counted: each mint or explicit claim bumps the
refcount; each release decrements it.
When the refcount reaches zero, the kernel claim is released and the
entry is removed from the authority's state.
.Pp
Policy claims
.Pq from Nm authorityd.conf
are immortal and cannot be released via the channel.
Release attempts return
.Er EPERM ,
which
.Xr serviced 8
silently ignores.
.Pp
When
.Xr serviced 8
exits or crashes, all dynamic claims are swept: released from the
kernel and removed from the authority's state.
Policy claims survive across serviced restarts.
.Pp
On configuration reload
.Pq Dv SIGHUP ,
dynamic claims are carried forward.
If a dynamic claim now appears in the reloaded configuration, it is
upgraded to a policy claim and becomes immortal.
.Pp
.Xr authorityctl 8
.Cm status
annotates each claim with its provenance:
.Ql [policy]
for manifest claims or
.Ql [service, refcount=N]
for dynamic claims.
.Bl -tag -width "network"
.It Va paths
Array of file and directory paths to claim.
Claiming a file blocks open, stat, chmod, chown, and other
vnode operations.
Claiming a directory blocks lookup into the subtree,
preventing access to all files within.
Default: empty.
.It Va network
Array of network endpoint objects to claim.
Each object has:
.Va port
(integer, range string such as
.Dq 80-8000 ,
.Dq *
for all ports, or
.Dq .\&<1024
for privileged ports),
.Va protocol
.Pq Dq tcp , Dq udp , Dq any , No or Dq * ,
.Va direction
.Pq Dq bind , Dq connect , Dq any , No or Dq * ,
and optionally
.Va domain
.Pq Dq inet , Dq inet6 , Dq any , No or Dq * ; No default is Dq inet
and
.Va address
(CIDR notation or
.Dq * ;
optional).
Foreign nonces receive
.Er EACCES
on bind or connect to claimed endpoints.
Default: empty.
.It Va jails
Array of jail claims.
Each element may be an integer JID, a string jail name, or an
object with:
.Va jid
(integer),
.Va name
(string),
.Va actions
.Pq Dq * No or array of Dq create , Dq get , Dq set , Dq remove , Dq attach ,
and optionally
.Va path
(jail root path).
Default: empty.
.It Va system
Array of system operation names to gate via the
.Xr mac_capability_system 4
service.
Once claimed, even root is denied unless holding an authorized
token from
.Nm .
Available operations:
.Dq kldload ,
.Dq kldunload ,
.Dq kldstat ,
.Dq reboot ,
.Dq swapon ,
.Dq swapoff ,
.Dq sysctl ,
.Dq kenv ,
.Dq kenv_read ,
.Dq acct ,
.Dq audit .
Default: empty (no system operations gated).
.El
.Sh CONTROL SOCKET
.Nm
listens on a Unix domain socket at
.Pa /var/run/authorityd.sock
(mode 0700 by default) for administrative commands.
The socket accepts at most 16 concurrent connections with a
2-second timeout per operation.
The protocol version is 1.
.Pp
The following operations are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "CTL_OP_SHUTDOWN (1)"
.It Dv CTL_OP_SHUTDOWN (1)
Initiate graceful shutdown.
Root only.
.It Dv CTL_OP_STATUS (2)
Query daemon status, active claims, and integrity flags.
Any user.
.It Dv CTL_OP_RELOAD (3)
Reload configuration, update claims, and forward
.Dv SIGHUP
to
.Xr serviced 8 .
Root only.
.El
.Pp
Service management commands (check, load, services) are handled by
.Xr serviced 8
via
.Xr servicectl 8 .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Nm
registers the following signals so that a process-descriptor supervisor can
request reload or graceful shutdown with
.Xr pdkill 2 .
Foreign-nonce ambient PID-based delivery is denied by mandatory capability
protection.
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM, SIGINT"
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload configuration, update claims (acquiring new claims and
releasing removed ones), and forward
.Dv SIGHUP
to
.Xr serviced 8 .
.It Dv SIGTERM , SIGINT
Initiate graceful shutdown.
The authority first signals
.Xr serviced 8
through its process descriptor and waits for it to drain managed services.
If
.Nm
exits unexpectedly, the kernel closes the last reference to the non-daemon
process descriptor and terminates the exact serviced instance.
As that process exits, its confined coalition descriptors close and terminate
the corresponding service processes and resources.
.It Dv SIGCHLD
Reap children and restart
.Xr serviced 8
according to the restart policy.
.El
.Pp
Descriptors delegated in protocol replies are restricted to
.Dv CAP_XFER_ONCE
before transmission.
Successful transmission consumes that state and installs the descriptor in
the receiver as
.Dv CAP_XFER_NONE .
Authority-owned capability descriptors are irreversibly restricted against
transfer, fork inheritance, and exec inheritance.
.Pp
Before launching a system-bundle service with
.Va kmod_requires ,
.Xr serviced 8
sends an exact-sized
.Dv AUTHORITY_OP_ENSURE_KMOD
request.
.Nm
temporarily claims
.Dv SYS_GATE_KLDSTAT | SYS_GATE_KLDLOAD ,
checks or loads the named module under its own nonce, releases the temporary
claim, and returns only status.
No module authority or token is delegated to
.Xr serviced 8 .
Module paths and malformed names are rejected.
.Pp
For each manifest
.Va capabilities.services
entry,
.Xr serviced 8
sends an exact-sized
.Dv AUTHORITY_OP_DELEGATE_SERVICE
request.
Only
.Dq mount ,
.Dq node ,
and
.Dq accounting ,
and
.Dq identity
are accepted.
The resulting descriptor is transferred once and arrives confined with
.Dv CAP_XFER_NONE ;
malformed or unknown requests are rejected.
.Pp
The serviced restart policy uses exponential backoff.
If
.Xr serviced 8
runs for at least 5 seconds, the crash counter resets and restart
is immediate.
If it crashes within 5 seconds, the delay starts at 1 second and
doubles up to a maximum of 30 seconds.
After 10 consecutive fast crashes, the circuit breaker trips and
.Nm
gives up restarting.
.Sh DTRACE PROBES
.Nm
is instrumented with DTrace USDT probes in the
.Ql authorityd
provider.
Probes are zero-cost when DTrace is not attached.
.Pp
.Em Lifecycle :
.Bl -tag -width "shutdown-done(duration_ns)" -compact
.It Li startup
Daemon initialization complete.
.It Li shutdown(reason)
Daemon shutting down.
Reason is a signal number or 0 for control socket shutdown.
.It Li shutdown-done(duration_ns)
Shutdown sequence complete.
.It Li config-load(path)
Configuration file parsed.
.El
.Pp
.Em Claims :
.Bl -tag -width "claim-net-release(port_min, port_max, protocol)" -compact
.It Li claim-path(path)
File or directory claimed successfully.
.It Li claim-path-fail(path)
File or directory claim failed.
.It Li claim-path-release(path)
Path claim released.
.It Li claim-net(port_min, port_max, protocol)
Network endpoint claimed.
.It Li claim-net-fail(port_min, port_max, protocol)
Network endpoint claim failed.
.It Li claim-net-release(port_min, port_max, protocol)
Network claim released.
.It Li claim-jail-release(name, actions)
Jail claim released.
.It Li claim-system-release(gates)
System gates released.
.El
.Pp
.Em Dynamic Claims :
.Bl -tag -width "dyn-release-net(port_min, port_max, protocol, refcount, result)" -compact
.It Li dyn-claim-path(path, result)
Dynamic path claim created or refcount bumped.
.It Li dyn-claim-net(port_min, port_max, protocol, result)
Dynamic network claim created or refcount bumped.
.It Li dyn-claim-jail(name, actions, result)
Dynamic jail claim created or refcount bumped.
.It Li dyn-claim-system(gates, result)
Dynamic system gate claim created or refcount bumped.
.It Li dyn-claim-vsock(cid, port_min, port_max, result)
Dynamic VSOCK endpoint claim created or refcount bumped.
.It Li dyn-release-path(path, refcount, result)
Dynamic path claim released.
Refcount is the value after decrement.
.It Li dyn-release-net(port_min, port_max, protocol, refcount, result)
Dynamic network claim released.
.It Li dyn-release-jail(name, actions, refcount, result)
Dynamic jail claim released.
.It Li dyn-release-system(gates, released, result)
Dynamic system gate claim released.
.Ar released
is the bitmask of gates whose refcount reached zero.
.It Li dyn-release-vsock(cid, port_min, port_max, refcount, result)
Dynamic VSOCK endpoint claim released.
.El
.Pp
.Em Integrity :
.Bl -tag -width "integrity(flags)" -compact
.It Li integrity(flags)
Capprotect integrity shield activated.
.El
.Pp
.Em Control :
.Bl -tag -width "ctl-cmd-done(op, uid, status, duration_ns)" -compact
.It Li ctl-accept(uid)
Control socket connection accepted.
.It Li ctl-cmd(op, uid)
Control command dispatched.
.It Li ctl-cmd-done(op, uid, status, duration_ns)
Control command completed.
.It Li ctl-deny(op, uid)
Control command denied (EPERM).
.El
.Pp
.Em Reload :
.Bl -tag -width "reload-claims-done(acquired, released, failed)" -compact
.It Li reload()
Configuration reload initiated.
.It Li reload-claims-start(nacquire, nrelease)
Claim delta computation complete.
.It Li reload-claims-done(acquired, released, failed)
Claim update complete.
.El
.Pp
.Em Minting :
.Bl -tag -width "mint-file(path, actions, result)" -compact
.It Li mint-path(path, result)
Path isolation token minted.
.It Li mint-file(path, actions, result)
Action-narrowed file isolation token minted.
.It Li mint-net(port_min, port_max, protocol, result)
Network isolation token minted.
.It Li mint-jail(jid, name, actions, result)
Jail isolation token minted.
.It Li mint-system(gates, result)
System gate token minted.
.It Li mint-vsock(cid, port_min, port_max, result)
VSOCK endpoint token minted.
.It Li create-jail(name, result)
Jail created.
.It Li channel-create(result)
Channel created.
.It Li coalition-create(result)
Coalition created.
.It Li kmod-ensure(name, result)
Pre-exec kernel module prerequisite checked or loaded.
.It Li service-delegate(name, result)
Named capability service descriptor delegated for a service launch.
.El
.Pp
.Em IPC :
.Bl -tag -width "ipc-dispatch-done(op, status, duration_ns)" -compact
.It Li ipc-recv(op)
Authority protocol message received from serviced.
.It Li ipc-reply(op, status)
Authority protocol reply sent.
.It Li ipc-dispatch-done(op, status, duration_ns)
Authority protocol dispatch complete.
.El
.Pp
.Em Bootstrap :
.Bl -tag -width "bootstrap-restart(count, delay_sec)" -compact
.It Li bootstrap-start(pid)
Serviced process started.
.It Li bootstrap-exit(pid, status)
Serviced process exited.
.It Li bootstrap-restart(count, delay_sec)
Serviced restart scheduled.
.El
.Pp
.Em Connections :
.Bl -tag -width "conn-count(nconns)" -compact
.It Li conn-count(nconns)
Control socket connection count changed.
.El
.Pp
.Em Errors :
.Bl -tag -width "error(subsys, msg)" -compact
.It Li error(subsys, msg)
Notable error.
.El
.Pp
Example: trace all minting operations:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtrace -n 'authorityd*:::mint-*'
.Ed
.Pp
Example: trace serviced lifecycle:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtrace -n 'authorityd*:::bootstrap-*'
.Ed
.Pp
Example: trace dynamic claim acquisition:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtrace -n 'authorityd*:::dyn-claim-* { printf("%s result=%d",
    copyinstr(arg0), arg1); }'
.Ed
.Pp
Example: trace dynamic claim release with refcount:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtrace -n 'authorityd*:::dyn-release-* { printf("refcount=%d result=%d",
    arg1, arg2); }'
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/libexec/serviced"
.It Pa /etc/authorityd.conf
Configuration file (UCL format).
Optional.
.It Pa /usr/libexec/serviced
Default service manager binary.
Started by
.Nm
as its single child process.
.It Pa /var/run/authorityd.pid
Default pidfile.
.It Pa /var/run/authorityd.sock
Default control socket (mode 0700).
.It Pa /dev/mac_capability
MAC_CAPABILITY control device, claimed exclusively by
.Nm
at startup.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Nm
exits with an error if the configuration file contains syntax errors,
if the pidfile cannot be acquired, or if required
.Xr mac_capability 4
operations fail.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Minimal configuration with default claims:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pidfile = "/var/run/authorityd.pid";
control_socket = "/var/run/authorityd.sock";
service_manager = "/usr/libexec/serviced";
.Ed
.Pp
Full integrity hardening (note: enabling
.Va signal
prevents
.Xr rc 8
from sending signals to
.Nm ) :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
integrity {
    ptrace = true;
    signal = true;
    visible = true;
    wait = true;
    sched = true;
    core = true;
    ktrace = true;
}
.Ed
.Pp
Claim sensitive files, a privileged port range, and system operations:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
claims {
    paths = [
        "/dev/mem",
        "/boot/kernel",
    ];
    network = [
        {
            port = ".<1024";
            protocol = "tcp";
            direction = "bind";
            domain = "inet";
            address = "192.0.2.0/24";
        },
    ];
    jails = [
        "webjail",
        {
            jid = 10;
            name = "dbjail";
            actions = ["create", "attach"];
            path = "/usr/local/jails/dbjail";
        },
    ];
    system = ["kldload", "kldunload", "kldstat",
              "reboot", "sysctl"];
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr procctl 2 ,
